WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:03.320
Film Courage: The ideal length of a YA novel?

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:04.320
Word count wise?

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:08.540
What’s the typical length and then if you
stretch it, what’s to be expected?

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:11.360
Jennifer Brody: That’s actually a great
question and that was something I was obsessed

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:16.150
about when I first started writing because
I know I tended to write long.

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.589
I know other people write shorter.

00:00:17.589 --> 00:00:26.019
I would say the sweet spot (at least in my
opinion) is somewhere between 75,000 and 85,000

00:00:26.019 --> 00:00:31.069
words for contemporary YA (which is a story
told in the here and now).

00:00:31.069 --> 00:00:35.660
You will see books that are shorter, so you
can even get away with 65,000 words.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.710
Or obviously longer than that.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:44.340
If you start to go above 100,000 words (and
my book definitely does), the first book is

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.960
somewhere in the 105,000 word count range
comparable to something like HUNGER GAMES.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:54.530
As the series progresses where you will get
more leeway on word count, they do span upwards.

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:58.620
I’m looking at 120,000 words on the third
book.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.960
Like I said, when you’re doing big word
building genre books like sci fi fantasy,

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:06.190
you do get more leeway on word count regardless
of genre.

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:10.550
So you can get away with something that is
over 100,000 words.

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:15.920
But if you’ve never sold a book before and
you’re going on submission, I would caution

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:20.511
you on doing anything that is too much longer
than 100,000 to 105,000 because that’s a

00:01:20.511 --> 00:01:21.810
pretty hefty book.

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:27.260
That said…I mean everyone has sold things
that are different lengths.

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:33.920
And I always think that the word count should
be justified by the story.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:39.479
I did learn that when you write multiple POVs
that this will balloon your word count, that’s

00:01:39.479 --> 00:01:40.690
why GAME OF THRONES is so long.

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:43.380
I have a lot of empathy of George R.R.

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:44.380
Martin.

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:49.170
But there is a reason why his books are spanning
over a 1,000 pages because once he starts

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:53.560
telling all those multiple stories really
it’s going to expand it.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:57.380
But yeah, so the sweet spot for word count
is going to be somewhere in those ranges.

